The base-image fix is on main and tagged v0.2.1. Issue #72 stays open, because the four glibc CVEs it was opened for are still unfixed in Debian.

- **Merged:** the manager landed e7afac7..90f6715 (the digest move 0abbbb8 plus a STATE.md update) on the full gate set, and its build was green. The new base is Debian 13.8 (glibc 2.41-12+deb13u5, freetype +deb13u2). On trivy it clears the 15 advisories Debian has fixed.
- **v0.2.1:** I tagged it at 90f6715 and pushed it, since main has taken no features since v0.2.0. The release workflow was still running the gates on the tag when the run ended, so whether it published isn't confirmed yet: https://github.com/tacplus-dev/kernel/actions/runs/46158559459. I didn't run a separate `just gates` on main; I relied on the manager's full-gate build of the same commit.
- **Backport:** PR #78 against release/0.1 is a clean cherry-pick of the digest move. It has not been built yet; its CI will do that. Its description says to tag v0.1.8 once it merges.
- **Still open:** on 2026-11-28 the Debian tracker lists CVE-2026-121757, -121758, -124024 and -126765 as unfixed in every suite, including trixie 2.41-12+deb13u5. Trixie marks them minor (`<no-dsa>`), so a fix may only come in a point release. Distroless `:latest` is still the digest we now pin, so moving it again would clear nothing.

I posted this on the issue and set it to back off until 2026-12-12, or sooner if something changes. The next run checks the tracker and distroless again, confirms the release run passed, and tags v0.1.8 if #78 has merged.
